This package's model code (src/coastdiff/models/vendor/) is adapted from
NVIDIA PhysicsNeMo and its CorrDiff model implementation. NVIDIA
Corporation is the developer of that underlying two-stage regression +
diffusion model architecture, EDM diffusion preconditioning, and sampler
(originally physicsnemo.models.diffusion_unets, physicsnemo.diffusion, and
related components). This package's own code is not affiliated with or
endorsed by NVIDIA; it is a separate, independent work. It does not require
a PhysicsNeMo installation at runtime -- the relevant PhysicsNeMo source
(Apache-2.0) has been copied in and adapted (trimmed to the specific
architecture this package's checkpoints use; PhysicsNeMo's own
model-registry/checkpoint-format machinery replaced with a small
self-contained loader) rather than used as an external library. This adaptation's correctness was verified by
comparing it against the original PhysicsNeMo-backed implementation: every
vendored model's state_dict keys/shapes match the real checkpoints
exactly, and a full forward pass (including the stochastic diffusion
sampler) produces bit-for-bit identical output to the original on the same
input. See docs/ARCHITECTURE.md for details.

